    <title>Exceptional Engineering S1 - "Emergency Helicopter"</title>
    <desc>In Bavaria, engineers build the high-tech H145 rescue helicopter, while skilled pilots navigate extreme terrain to save lives.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261120231437 +0000" stop="20261121001617 +0000">
    <title>Exceptional Engineering S1 - "Harvesting Giants"</title>
    <desc>Inside the Fendt factory, advanced GPS technology and complex assembly lines create the world's most powerful 517-hp agricultural tractor.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121001617 +0000" stop="20261121011448 +0000">
    <title>Exceptional Engineering S1 - "Hightech in the Air"</title>
    <desc>The Airbus A350 proves its high-tech capabilities during a demanding 12-hour maiden long-haul flight from Munich to Hong Kong.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121011448 +0000" stop="20261121021806 +0000">
    <title>Bridging the Expanse S1 - "Baring All in Steel"</title>
    <desc>Engineers during the Great Depression design intricate skeletal steel structures, optimizing material efficiency to boost global economies.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121021806 +0000" stop="20261121032440 +0000">
    <title>Top 10: The Art of Architecture S1 - "Bridges: City Icons"</title>
    <desc>Here are ten of the world greatest modern bridges - engineering marvels and architectural masterpieces from around the world.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121032440 +0000" stop="20261121043027 +0000">
    <title>Top 10: The Art of Architecture S1 - "Transport Megastructures-Engineering Wonders"</title>
    <desc>The Trans-Siberian Railway, New York City Subway, Channel Tunnel and Suez Canal are only some of the breathtaking megastructures devised by humanity.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121043027 +0000" stop="20261121053609 +0000">
    <title>Top 10: The Art of Architecture S1 - "Museums and Galleries: Architectural Treasures"</title>
    <desc>Bilbao, Amsterdam, Antwerp and Florence belong to a dynamic group of cities that preserve the heritage of humanity through museums.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121053609 +0000" stop="20261121060000 +0000">
    <title>Bright Now S1 - "The Science of Cute"</title>
    <desc>Domestication shaped wolves into dogs and transformed both their behavior and their anatomy. New discoveries show how dogs produce a very specific eyebrow movement more often than wolves do.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121060000 +0000" stop="20261121070318 +0000">
    <title>Megastructures: Gardens By The Bay</title>
    <desc>Discover the making of Singapore’s Gardens by the Bay, where groundbreaking engineering created a spectacular urban oasis unlike any other.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121070318 +0000" stop="20261121073142 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Striker II, Navy Drones, F35B Fighter"</title>
    <desc>We have rare acces to BAE Systems. At their research centre in Kent, they're developing the futuristic Striker II helmet giving fighter pilots the edge in aerial combat</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121073142 +0000" stop="20261121075942 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Live Fire Exercises, Body Armor, Armored Vehicle AJAX"</title>
    <desc>Discover the latest innovations in kit and equipment at the key military and security exhibition in the UK; Lockheed Martin's heat-seeking Indago drone; and the tech spec on the British Army's new armored vehicle, the AJAX.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121075942 +0000" stop="20261121082724 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Battlefield 3-D, Drone Tech, 2-man Orcasub"</title>
    <desc>The innovative combination of 3D video and drone technology gives infantry soldiers an accurate battlefield picture. Northrop Grumman's top European executive shares their predictions on how technology will change the way we fight.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121082724 +0000" stop="20261121085547 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "USS Zumwalt, Tank Training, Special Forces Vehicle"</title>
    <desc>We reveal eye-witness intelligence on the USS Zumwalt, America's ultra-hi tech, four billion dollar guided missile destroyer. Learn more about the British firm who've developed Minerva, an ingenious, low-cost but realistic tank simulator.</desc>
  </programme>
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121085547 +0000" stop="20261121092347 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Typhoon Fighter, Combat Medics, USS Dwight D. Eisenhower"</title>
    <desc>The Military Tech Show captures the moment when BAE System's radical new pilot helmet, the Striker II, goes operational for the first time in a Typhoon fighter aircraft; how interactive technology is helping train military combat medics.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121092347 +0000" stop="20261121095207 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Spear 3 Missile, Battlefield VR, Spy Drones"</title>
    <desc>European manufacturer MBDA give a hands-on demonstration of their state-of-the-art missile, the Spear 3. Learn how scientists are using a virtual reality headset to see the battlefield in a revealing new way.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121095207 +0000" stop="20261121102029 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Radar Tech, Imperial War Museum, Land Mine Detection"</title>
    <desc>We have rare access to the German Aerospace Center outside Munich where scientists are using new forms of radar for surveillance and detecting land mines.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121102029 +0000" stop="20261121104854 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "RAF Station, Typhoon Squadron, The Flight Deck"</title>
    <desc>We're at Royal Air Force station Brize Norton, Oxfordshire, where we've been given an exclusive look at the RAF's ground-breaking, multi-role refuelling and transporter aircraft, the Voyager.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121104854 +0000" stop="20261121111712 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Targeting &amp; Tracking, Navigation, Seagoing Drones"</title>
    <desc>We reveal an experimental sensor, monitoring and targeting system developed for troops by the UK's Defence Science and Technology Laboratory and Roke Manor Research. The iXblue Marins navigation black box guides navy ships.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121111712 +0000" stop="20261121114533 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "NATO Maritime Centre, No Shipping-No Shopping"</title>
    <desc>We visit NATO's Centre for Maritime Research and Experimentation in La Spezia, Italy. We learn how the world's oceans are one of the last places that military technology can be hidden from prying eyes.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121114533 +0000" stop="20261121121349 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Terrorist Threats, Sea Wasp Robot, Combat Medics"</title>
    <desc>With an increasing terrorist threat to ports and shipping, the Swedish manufacturer SAAB has developed the Sea Wasp, an under-water robot for detecting explosive devices.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121121349 +0000" stop="20261121124204 +0000">
    <title>The Military Tech Show S1 - "Warrior Vehicles, British Special Forces"</title>
    <desc>We're in Scotland for Unmanned Warrior, the key international military exercise using unmanned underwater, surface and airborne vehicles. We visit the Italian textile manufacturer who's kitting from a revolutionary new form of wool.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121124204 +0000" stop="20261121134520 +0000">
    <title>Cold War: The Tech Race S1 - "Fuel for Destruction"</title>
    <desc>The atomic age introduces powerful rockets and nuclear energy, balancing technological advancement with threats like the Chernobyl disaster.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121134520 +0000" stop="20261121144835 +0000">
    <title>Cold War: The Tech Race S1 - "Golden Age of Science"</title>
    <desc>Military funding drives a boom in earth sciences and biological research, creating advanced weapons alongside deeper insights into our world.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121144835 +0000" stop="20261121155152 +0000">
    <title>Cold War: The Tech Race S1 - "Information Is Power"</title>
    <desc>Cold War secrecy accelerates spy tech, satellite surveillance, and early computer networks, laying the foundation for modern global communications.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261121155152 +0000" stop="20261121165508 +0000">
    <title>Cold War: The Tech Race S1 - "Race to Space"</title>
    <desc>Superpower rivalries turn missile tech toward orbital supremacy, driving historic milestones from early satellite launches to landing on the moon.</desc>
  </programme>
  
